  "description": "Clingy, velvety sauce, starchy noodles, and fresh vegetables.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 1 hr 20 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: 1 tablespoon chile garlic sauce (optional); Toasted sesame seeds, coarsely ground using a mortar and pestle, for serving\n\nNotes: Chinese sesame paste, unlike most commercially available tahini, is always made with toasted sesame seeds.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The vinaigrette can be made up to 1 week in advance; keep refrigerated in an airtight container.\nThe noodles, once tossed in the sauce, will hold up to 1 day in the refrigerator, but any longer and the noodles will lose their textural quality.",
